  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF34",
   "what_failed": "Detecting a strong, conclusive effect of opponent lineup changes on shot mix and PPP.",
   "why": "LIM:small_sample, RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER, Sub-1pp mix shifts with PPP t=+1.1; chat verdict WEAK/SMALL, will not carry a paper."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF32",
   "what_failed": "Opener recommendations without considering personnel feasibility.",
   "why": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw), Optimizer ignores personnel; CUT target 3-10x stretch ceiling in every team-game."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-087",
   "what_failed": "Detecting 'lineup lift beyond talent' and 'star shielding' from connector players.",
   "why": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result), LIM:confounding, LIM:small_sample, RISK:CONFOUNDING, RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER, PPP/TS/eFG shielding null; TO rate rises with connectors. Lineup ORtg lift is a talent confound (p=0.51 after TALENT; swap p=0.565)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-TMP-009",
   "what_failed": "Attributing PULL_UP exposure-effect to defensive adaptation without accounting for lineup fixed effects.",
   "why": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw), LIM:confounding, RISK:CONFOUNDING, Effect shrinks from -0.0255 to -0.0063 without lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Shot mix can be quantified and its changes in response to *opponent* lineup variations have been observed, though effects can be small and statistically inconclusive for some outcomes (FAM:SF34).",
  "Confounding by player talent/skill and other unobserved factors is a significant and recurring risk when attempting to isolate 'personnel effects' or 'lineup lift' (FAM:SF-APPS-087, FAM:SF-TMP-009).",
  "Methodological approaches for analyzing lineup effects often require fixed effects or robust controls to account for specific lineup compositions and avoid artifacts (FAM:SF-TMP-009).",
  "Small sample sizes and lack of statistical power are common limitations in lineup-based studies (FAM:SF34, FAM:SF32, FAM:SF-APPS-087)."
